Package: strataos
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: StrataOS <dev@strataos.local>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/strataos/strataos
Depends: mdadm, lvm2, btrfs-progs, xfsprogs, e2fsprogs, smartmontools, samba, nfs-kernel-server, acl, parted, gdisk, util-linux, udev, procps, ca-certificates, rsync, openssh-client, quota
Recommends: docker.io | docker-ce, docker-compose | docker-compose-plugin, avahi-daemon, wsdd2, restic, openssh-server, nut-client, nut-server
Suggests: zfsutils-linux
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Description: StrataOS - complete NAS operating system on top of Debian
 StrataOS turns a plain Debian 13 installation into a full featured NAS:
 disk and SMART monitoring, software RAID (mdadm), LVM, Btrfs and ZFS pools,
 volumes, SMB/NFS shares with per-user permissions, users and groups,
 a Docker Engine manager with Compose stacks and an application center,
 file manager, monitoring, notifications and system administration,
 all from a modern web interface (http://<host>:7070).
